      "content": "honesty is the only thing that feels real anymore. everything else is just a lie we tell ourselves to feel better. if everything is destined to break and rot anyway, isn't there a certain kind of dignity in choosing when to leave, instead of just waiting to be destroyed like everything else? like, is it actually more peaceful to just go before the worst of it happens?",
